speechtext:
I cannot at all object to it, but I want to know if the same result as takes place in the Quebec or Montreal district will eventually take place at St. John, Halifax and other Maritime province ports;

Supply-Marine and Fisheries
that is, when 1a pilot is pensioned, will he fall on this general fund, or even though the minister takes charge will it remain a purely local matter?

WThat evidence is there that any of those fishways were in any way defective? I have heard a great deal about this, and I know from my experience in the department that fishways are constantly put in; but it seems to me that, though every effort should be made to permit fish to pass upstream for spawning, too many restrictions are being put on industry. Requests are made for fishways here and fishways there;

Supply-Marine and Fisheries
or the statement is made that sawdust is getting in a stream here and sawdust is getting in a stream there, and people are compelled to install a fishway, according to plans and specifications supplied by the department, for the purpose of letting one or two fish get up stream, irrespective of the damage this is doing to industry.
